=== P3 Feature view 0143 HeroGauges (Android) ===
date: 2026-06-12T02:25:55.5019090-07:00
capability: Jetpack Compose + Material 3 present; Kotlin 2.4.0 (supersedes prompt's 2.2.x floor); JDK 21 (Android Studio JBR); Android SDK present (ANDROID_HOME). Build/test/lint all run on this runner.
note: settings.gradle.kts maps the single app module to Gradle path ':android' (sources under app/); the prompt gate's ':app:' is the source dir, so the working task path is ':android:' (same mapping the A-0058/A-0103 predecessor logs documented).
note: surface-name collision - three web HeroGauges (analytics A-0058 / charging A-0103 / driving A-0143) map to one native dir com/teslasync/feature-views/HeroGauges. A-0058 (HeroGauges) and A-0103 (ChargingHeroGauges, .charging sub-package) are committed predecessors, left intact (honesty covenant #7). This A-0143 driving port adds DrivingHeroGauges in the .driving sub-package; diagnostics SLUG stays the prompt surface slug 'HeroGauges'.
note: web source web/src/features/driving/components/drive-detail/HeroGauges.tsx - GlassPanel > flex-wrap centered row (native FlowRow) of four RadialGauges (Distance/Max Speed/Duration/Consumption) + a conditional fifth (Efficiency, only when stats.efficiencyPctPer100 != null). Distance/duration arrive SI and are converted here (convertDistanceFromSI, /60); max-speed + efficiency-percent arrive pre-converted from the owning page's computeStats (exactly as the web component receives them); consumption Wh/km -> Wh/mi via KM_PER_MILE. Values rounded (Math.round / Number(fmtNumber)) and clamped to [0,max], decimals per the web RadialGauge isInteger(clamped)?0:precision rule.
note: cache/network states (loading/stale/offline/error) live on the owning drive-detail page, not on this presentational child - the same boundary the A-0058/A-0103 ports document; a null prop renders the four zero gauges so the surface is never blank.
note: tests added under app/src/test/java/io/teslasync/android/featureviews/herogauges/driving (Projection + Diagnostics); the projection doubles as the per-state snapshot + a11y label/value check, mirroring the A-0058/A-0103 predecessor test shape.
